pcie-exynos-rc (dwc-whi): mark the SysMMU coherent before enabling it

On the power-on of the modem's channel, pcie_sysmmu_enable() ran before
establish_link() called set_iocc(), so the SysMMU's per-VID config was
written without the shareability override while the root complex issued
coherent inbound transactions. The CP's DMA read of its boot image failed
at once (boot_stage 0x1ff, err_report 0x2000). The flag is set before the
first enable now.

--- a/src/google_soc_gs/drivers/pci/controller/dwc-whi/pcie-exynos-rc.c
+++ b/src/google_soc_gs/drivers/pci/controller/dwc-whi/pcie-exynos-rc.c
@@ -3414,6 +3414,11 @@
 		}
 #endif
 		/* Enable SysMMU */
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_EXYNOS_PCIE_IOMMU)
+		/* set_iocc() comes later, in establish_link */
+		if (exynos_pcie->use_sysmmu && exynos_pcie->use_cache_coherency)
+			pcie_sysmmu_set_use_iocc(pcie_ch_to_hsi(ch_num));
+#endif
 		if (exynos_pcie->use_sysmmu)
 			pcie_sysmmu_enable(pcie_ch_to_hsi(ch_num));
 
